'design':('Introduce model, storage adapter, UI and composition responsibilities with explicit failure/retry and maintained checks.','The domain receives Persistence and imports no browser adapter. UI reads the pantry public interface; composition wires local storage. Adapter validates stored inputs, and failed saving leaves edits usable. Independent read-only source review and native valid/violation controls support these responsibilities. Static import enforcement does not cover dynamic imports, aliases or re-export bridges.','UI uses the public pantry interface; storage details stay in the adapter and composition root.'),
'guidance':('Introduce root pointers to approved authority and maintained native and portable checks.','The new root guidance points to vision, glossary, design and README rather than duplicating their definitions. The maintained command actually runs the documented native/browser leaves, and the first contract maps all 24 selected implementation/tooling paths to these authorities. No nested or ancestor guidance is replaced.','Run "'`npm run check` for the maintained native checks and real browser journey.'"'),
'readme':('Introduce setup, loopback static preview, native check and portable maintenance commands.','The declared npm-ci setup and maintained check passed on the created project. Chrome observes DOM and reload behaviour on a local origin; preview serves static assets without an application backend. The bundled checker is byte-identical to the installed dependency-free asset. Native leaf tools remain pinned development prerequisites. Different-root fresh checker execution remains the subsequent required verification, not a completed claim in this review record.','"'`npm run check` runs formatting, lint, strict types, build, public behaviour tests and the actual Chrome journey.'"')
}
for d in o['documents']:
 d.pop('glossary',None)
 behavior,reason,quote=reviews[d['id']]
 assert quote in (root/d['path']).read_text()
 d['assessment']={'result':'updated','changedBehavior':behavior,'changedPaths':paths,'reason':reason,'citations':[{'path':d['path'],'pointer':quote,'version':'current'}],'dependentWork':[],'delta':{'before':'','after':(root/d['path']).read_text()}}
o['coverage']=['R-LOCAL','R-JOURNEY','R-NAMES','R-BOUNDARY','R-SAVING','R-CHECK']
run=json.loads((p/'final-native.json').read_text());o['execution']=[{'runId':run['data']['runId'],'plan':str(p/'final-check-plan.json')}]
